  { number := 64, text := "## 3. Terms" },
  { number := 65, text := "" },
  { number := 66, text := "1. A session is one running `grok-oss` text user interface process." },
  { number := 67, text := "2. An outside agent is a program that is not that session and that uses the bus client in Clause 4.2." },
  { number := 68, text := "3. `TOON` is the notation the source draft names through `util/toon` and `GROK_TOOL_RESULT_FORMAT`. This specification does not redefine that notation." },
  { number := 69, text := "4. Attach means open the socket of a session that is already running. Attach does not start a new session." },
  { number := 70, text := "5. `ACP` names the internal agent client protocol the source draft records as already present inside `grok-oss`. This specification does not replace `ACP`." },
  { number := 71, text := "" },
  { number := 72, text := "## 4. Requirements" },
  { number := 73, text := "" },
  { number := 74, text := "The keywords MUST, MUST NOT, REQUIRED, SHALL, SHALL NOT, SHOULD, SHOULD NOT, RECOMMENDED, MAY, and OPTIONAL in this document are to be interpreted as described in RFC 2119." },
  { number := 75, text := "" },
  { number := 76, text := "### 4.1 Baseline the source draft records (informative)" },
  { number := 77, text := "" },
  { number := 78, text := "This subsection is informative. It records what the source draft says already exists in `grok-oss`. Those sentences are not a conformance claim that this repository proved those commands. They are not a claim that a session bus program exists." },
  { number := 79, text := "" },
  { number := 80, text := "1. The draft records internal `ACP` (`app/acp_handler`, `session/acp_session_impl`). The draft records that `grok-oss agent stdio` runs a new agent over `stdio`." },
  { number := 81, text := "2. The draft records `grok-oss running` with fields for process id, session id, working directory, state, model, and `subagents`. The draft also records `sessions`, `export`, and `leader list` and `leader info`." },
  { number := 82, text := "3. The draft records `util/toon` and `GROK_TOOL_RESULT_FORMAT` with values `auto`, `toon`, and `json`." },
  { number := 83, text := "4. The draft records the gap: there is no way to attach to a text user interface session that is already running. An outside agent that only sees `grok-oss running` sees a summary of one line." },
  { number := 84, text := "" },
  { number := 85, text := "### 4.2 Socket and client" },
  { number := 86, text := "" },
  { number := 87, text := "1. Each running text user interface session MUST own one local socket." },
  { number := 88, text := "2. The socket path MUST be `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/grok-oss/<session>.sock`." },
  { number := 89, text := "3. The socket mode MUST be `0600`." },
  { number := 90, text := "4. The socket MUST allow the same user id only. The socket MUST NOT allow a different user id." },
  { number := 91, text := "5. The bus MUST NOT open a network listener." },
  { number := 92, text := "6. The client MUST be `grok-oss bus`. The form MUST be `grok-oss bus <method> [session] [fields]` over `stdio`." },
  { number := 93, text := "7. The client MUST use `TOON` for input and for output." },
  { number := 94, text := "8. A `stdio` server invoked as `grok-oss mcp-serve bus` MUST expose the same methods as tools, so Grok Bot and any `MCP` client can call them." },
  { number := 95, text := "" },
  { number := 96, text := "### 4.3 Methods" },
  { number := 97, text := "" },
  { number := 98, text := "A conforming bus MUST provide each method in this list. The tier names are the names in the source draft. This document does not add methods the draft does not name." },
  { number := 99, text := "" },
  { number := 100, text := "1. `sessions` returns the session id, the working directory, the repository and branch, the state (idle, working, or waiting for approval), the model, `subagents`, and the last activity. The tier is compact." },
  { number := 101, text := "2. `look` returns the current goal, the plan and `todos`, summaries of the last N turns, a pending approval, and the files `git` reports as dirty. The tier MAY be compact, room, or rich." },
  { number := 102, text := "3. `transcript` returns turns since the cursor `since:<turn_id>`. Those turns MUST be deltas only. The tier is rich." },
  { number := 103, text := "4. `owns` returns which session, if any, is working in a given path or repository. The tier is compact." },
  { number := 104, text := "5. `interject` injects a message into the running turn. That injection is the same as typing during the current turn. The tier is act." },
  { number := 105, text := "6. `queue` places a prompt to run after the current turn. The tier is act." },
  { number := 106, text := "7. `approve` and `deny` answer a pending permission prompt by id. The tier is act, and the pair is gated as in Clause 4.4." },
  { number := 107, text := "8. `subscribe` streams state changes for turn start, turn end, approval needed, and error. The tier is event." },
  { number := 108, text := "" },
  { number := 109, text := "### 4.4 Safety" },
  { number := 110, text := "" },
  { number := 111, text := "1. The socket rules in Clause 4.2 items 4 and 5 are REQUIRED." },
  { number := 112, text := "2. A session MAY set `bus.readonly` to true. The source draft names that flag and does not state a further effect. This specification does not invent that effect." },
  { number := 113, text := "3. `approve` MUST be off by default. The configuration key the draft names is `[bus] allow_approve = false` in `~/.grok/config.toml`." },
  { number := 114, text := "4. `deny` is gated with `approve` in the source draft. `deny` MUST be off by default. The draft does not name a separate configuration key for `deny`." },
  { number := 115, text := "5. Every act from an outside agent MUST be shown in the text user interface as `[bus: <client>]` followed by the act text, so the person at the keyboard can see who steered the session." },
  { number := 116, text := "6. The bus MUST NOT reboot a session. The bus MUST NOT restart a service. The bus MUST NOT kill a session." },
  { number := 117, text := "7. Steer methods (`interject`, `queue`, `approve`, and `deny`) MUST use the same permissions a person at that text user interface has. This document does not claim those methods are implemented." },
  { number := 118, text := "" },
  { number := 119, text := "### 4.5 Token budget" },
  { number := 120, text := "" },
  { number := 121, text := "1. A bus reply MUST be compact by default." },
  { number := 122, text := "2. Text fields returned by `look` MUST be capped at 80 characters. The source draft names that cap as the same style as `OUTLINE_STRING_MAX`." },
  { number := 123, text := "3. `transcript` MUST return deltas from a cursor. `transcript` MUST NOT return the full session text." },
  { number := 124, text := "" },
  { number := 125, text := "### 4.6 Success criteria" },
  { number := 126, text := "" },
  { number := 127, text := "A program that claims conformance to this specification MUST meet every item in this list. This document does not claim that such a program exists." },
  { number := 128, text := "" },
  { number := 129, text := "1. An outside agent can list sessions and can read each session plan without scraping." },
  { number := 130, text := "2. Before that outside agent launches coding work, it can call `owns` and defer to the live session that already owns that repository." },
  { number := 131, text := "3. `interject` and `queue` round trip, and the text user interface shows the attribution in Clause 4.4 item 5." },
  { number := 132, text := "4. A default install exposes no network surface and does not approve by itself." },
  { number := 133, text := "" },
  { number := 134, text := "### 4.7 Out of scope" },
  { number := 135, text := "" },
  { number := 136, text := "1. Remote access and network access are out of scope. Clause 4.2 item 5 already forbids a network listener." },
  { number := 137, text := "2. Replacing `ACP` is out of scope." },
  { number := 138, text := "3. Letting an outside agent change permissions or change configuration is out of scope." },
  { number := 139, text := "" },
  { number := 140, text := "### 4.8 Work the source draft names and this document does not claim is done" },
  { number := 141, text := "" },
  { number := 142, text := "This subsection records work streams from the source draft. None of these items is claimed done. A parenthetical file name here is not the residual record. Clause 6 is the residual record." },
  { number := 143, text := "" },
  { number := 144, text := "1. The draft calls the plan itself work stream W0 and says it is done when that plan is merged. This repository does not record that merge." },
  { number := 145, text := "2. Work stream W1 is a socket for each session in the text user interface, plus `sessions` and `look`. The draft says this is done when `grok-oss bus sessions` matches `grok-oss running`. That match is not claimed here." },
  { number := 146, text := "3. Work stream W2 is `transcript` deltas plus `owns`. The draft says an outside agent can then tell that a session owns `~/Projects/surmount/colibri`. That check is not claimed here." },
  { number := 147, text := "4. Work stream W3 is `interject` and `queue`, plus the attribution line in the text user interface. The draft says an interjection lands during the current turn and is visible. That landing is not claimed here." },
  { number := 148, text := "5. Work stream W4 is `subscribe` events. The draft says an event that approval is needed reaches the client in less than one second. That timing is not claimed here." },
  { number := 149, text := "6. Work stream W5 is `mcp-serve bus` over `stdio`. The draft says Grok Bot calls `look` through `MCP`. That call is not claimed here." },
  { number := 150, text := "7. Work stream W6 is gated `approve` and `deny`. The draft says the gate is off by default and that tests cover the denial path. Those tests are not in this repository." },
  { number := 151, text := "8. The draft says product tests are Rust tests in `xai-grok-shell`, in the same style as `test_leader_stdio_integration`, and that there is no Python driver. This repository does not contain those Rust tests and does not add a Python driver." },
  { number := 152, text := "" },
  { number := 153, text := "## 5. Required Conformance" },
  { number := 154, text := "" },
  { number := 155, text := "Required conformance to this specification holds if and only if every item in this list holds." },
  { number := 156, text := "" },
  { number := 157, text := "1. This specification is number 0015 and the file name is `0015_Session_Bus.md` (Clause 1)." },
  { number := 158, text := "2. Each running text user interface session owns a local socket at `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/grok-oss/<session>.sock` with mode `0600`, the same user id only, and no network listener (Clause 4.2)." },
  { number := 159, text := "3. The client is `grok-oss bus` over `stdio` with `TOON` in both directions, and `grok-oss mcp-serve bus` exposes the same methods as tools (Clause 4.2)." },
  { number := 160, text := "4. The methods are `sessions`, `look`, `transcript`, `owns`, `interject`, `queue`, `approve`, `deny`, and `subscribe`, with the tiers and results in Clause 4.3." },
  { number := 161, text := "5. `approve` and `deny` are off by default. `transcript` returns deltas only and does not return the full text. The bus does not kill a session (Clause 4.3, Clause 4.4, and Clause 4.5)." },
  { number := 162, text := "6. Replies are compact by default, and `look` field text is capped at 80 characters (Clause 4.5)." },
  { number := 163, text := "7. Remote access, replacing `ACP`, and outside changes to permissions or configuration are out of scope (Clause 4.7)." },
  { number := 164, text := "8. A conforming session bus program is not claimed (Clause 1 and Clause 4.6)." },
  { number := 165, text := "9. Numbered markdown remains the contract humans read. Lean spec encodings are not that markdown. Lean proofs are not the specification. A mash of spec encodings and their proofs in one module does not conform in this repository (Clause 1.2)." },
  { number := 166, text := "" },
  { number := 167, text := "This specification is not itself a conforming session bus program. Meeting these items is a claim about a program that claims this specification. It is not a claim that this markdown file is that program." },
  { number := 168, text := "" },
  { number := 169, text := "Optional items (MAY, the unread effect of `bus.readonly`, and the informative baseline in Clause 4.1) do not break conformance when unmet." },
  { number := 170, text := "" },
  { number := 171, text := "## 6. Residual" },
